    "body": "## Description\nThe contract calculates DOMAIN_SEPARATOR only once, at constructor execution, and stores it as an immutable variable. The contract uses block.chainid during deployment for this calculation.\n```\n    constructor() {\n        DOMAIN_SEPARATOR = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                // ...\n                block.chainid, // Chain ID during deployment\n                address(this)\n            )\n        );\n    }\n```\nHowever, in the _verifyAndMarkIntent function, the logic for creating the struct hash (intentHash) includes the chainid() opcode which is dynamic (retrieving the current Chain ID):\n```\n            // ...\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0xc0), chainid()) // Dynamic chain ID at execution time\n            // ...\n```\nLogical Bug:\nIf a blockchain experiences a hard fork or a network ID change (which is common in EVM chains), the block.chainid will change.\n1. The user's wallet (client-side such as Metamask/Ethers.js) will detect the new chain ID and generate a signature based on the new DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (as per the EIP-712 standard).\n2. The contract will verify the signature using:\n- OLD DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (because it is immutable).\n- NEW chainid (in the intentHash).\nA mismatch between the user's (new) DOMAIN_SEPARATOR and the contract's (old) DOMAIN_SEPARATOR will cause the ECDSA.recover function to return an incorrect address or fail. Consequently, all contract features will be DoSed, and no valid transactions can be processed post-fork.\n\nImpacted Code:\n1.\tConstructor: Sets DOMAIN_SEPARATOR statically.\n```\nconstructor() {\n        DOMAIN_SEPARATOR = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\"),\n                keccak256(bytes(\"TrailsIntentEntrypoint\")),\n                keccak256(bytes(VERSION)),\n                block.chainid,\n                address(this)\n            )\n        );\n    }\n```\n2.\tFunction _verifyAndMarkIntent: Combines static DOMAIN_SEPARATOR with dynamic hash.\n```\n        bytes32 _domainSeparator = DOMAIN_SEPARATOR; // Still using old post-fork values\n        bytes32 digest;\n        assembly {\n            // ...\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x20), _domainSeparator)\n            // ...\n        }\n```\n## Impact\n1. Protocol Bricking: If the Chain ID changes, the contract becomes permanently useless because it cannot verify a new valid signature.\n2. Mismatch with the Standard: This implementation violates the EIP-712 recommendation, which recommends recalculating the DOMAIN_SEPARATOR if the chain ID changes to prevent inter-chain replay attacks and ensure post-fork validity.\n\n## Recommendation\nUse the latest Solady/OpenZeppelin standard pattern to dynamically calculate DOMAIN_SEPARATOR if the chainid changes:\n```\n    // Save chainId during deployment\n    uint256 internal immutable _INITIAL_CHAIN_ID;\n    bytes32 internal immutable _INITIAL_DOMAIN_SEPARATOR;\n\n    constructor() {\n        _INITIAL_CHAIN_ID = block.chainid;\n        _INITIAL_DOMAIN_SEPARATOR = _computeDomainSeparator();\n    }\n\n    function _computeDomainSeparator() internal view returns (bytes32) {\n        return keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\"),\n                keccak256(bytes(\"TrailsIntentEntrypoint\")),\n                keccak256(bytes(VERSION)),\n                block.chainid, // Always fetch the current chainid\n                address(this)\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function DOMAIN_SEPARATOR() public view returns (bytes32) {\n        // If the chainid is the same as when deploying, return the cache. If different, recalculate.\n        return block.chainid == _INITIAL_CHAIN_ID ? _INITIAL_DOMAIN_SEPARATOR : _computeDomainSeparator();\n    }",
    "proof_of_concept": "## PoC\nAdd test file *.t.sol\n```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport {TrailsIntentEntrypoint} from \"../src/TrailsIntentEntrypoint.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Permit} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/ERC20Permit.sol\";\nimport {MockNonStandardERC20} from \"./mocks/MockNonStandardERC20.sol\";\n\n// Mock ERC20 token with permit functionality for testing\ncontract MockERC20Permit is ERC20, ERC20Permit {\n    constructor() ERC20(\"Mock Token\", \"MTK\") ERC20Permit(\"Mock Token\") {\n        _mint(msg.sender, 1000000 * 10 ** decimals());\n    }\n}\n\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Test Contract\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncontract TrailsIntentEntrypointTest is Test {\n    // Mirror events for expectEmit if needed\n    event FeePaid(address indexed user, address indexed feeToken, uint256 feeAmount, address indexed feeCollector);\n    event IntentDeposit(address indexed user, address indexed intentAddress, uint256 amount);\n    \n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Test State Variables\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    TrailsIntentEntrypoint public entrypoint;\n    MockERC20Permit public token;\n    address public user = vm.addr(0x123456789);\n    uint256 public userPrivateKey = 0x123456789;\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        entrypoint = new TrailsIntentEntrypoint();\n        token = new MockERC20Permit();\n        // Give user some tokens and check transfer success\n        assertTrue(token.transfer(user, 1000 * 10 ** token.decimals()));\n    }\n    function test_ChainForkCausesPermanentDoSDueToImmutableDomainSeparator() public {\n        console.log(\"=== PHASE 1: BEFORE HARD FORK ===\");\n        console.log(\"Initial chainId:\", block.chainid);\n        \n        address intentAddress = address(0x999);\n        address feeCollector = address(0x888);\n        uint256 depositAmount = 100 * 10 ** token.decimals();\n        uint256 feeAmount = 10 * 10 ** token.decimals();\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 1 hours;\n        uint256 intentNonce = 0;\n\n        // Approve tokens\n        vm.prank(user);\n        token.approve(address(entrypoint), type(uint256).max);\n\n        // User creates signature BEFORE fork (chainId = current)\n        (uint8 sigV1, bytes32 sigR1, bytes32 sigS1) = \n            _signIntent2(user, depositAmount, intentAddress, deadline, intentNonce, feeAmount, feeCollector);\n\n        console.log(\"DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (immutable):\", vm.toString(entrypoint.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR()));\n        console.log(\"User signed with chainId:\", block.chainid);\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // Verify signature works BEFORE fork\n        vm.prank(feeCollector);\n        entrypoint.depositToIntent(\n            user,\n            address(token),\n            depositAmount,\n            intentAddress,\n            deadline,\n            intentNonce,\n            feeAmount,\n            feeCollector,\n            sigV1,\n            sigR1,\n            sigS1\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"Transaction succeeded before fork\");\n        console.log(\"Tokens deposited to intent address:\", token.balanceOf(intentAddress));\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // ==================== PHASE 2: HARD FORK OCCURS ====================\n        console.log(\"=== PHASE 2: HARD FORK OCCURS ===\");\n        \n        // Simulate hard fork: chainId changes from 31337 to 10001\n        uint256 newChainId = 10001;\n        vm.chainId(newChainId);\n        \n        console.log(\"HARD FORK HAPPENED!\");\n        console.log(\"New chainId:\", block.chainid);\n        console.log(\"DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (still old):\", vm.toString(entrypoint.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR()));\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // ==================== PHASE 3: USER TRIES TO TRANSACT AFTER FORK ====================\n        console.log(\"=== PHASE 3: USER ATTEMPTS TRANSACTION AFTER FORK ===\");\n        \n        // Setup new transaction (nonce incremented)\n        address intentAddress2 = address(0x888);\n        uint256 intentNonce2 = 1; // Next nonce\n        \n        // User creates NEW signature with NEW chainId (as wallet would do)\n        // Wallet (Metamask, etc) will use NEW chainId for DOMAIN_SEPARATOR\n        console.log(\"User wallet creates signature with NEW chainId:\", block.chainid);\n        \n        // This is what user WOULD sign (with new chainId in DOMAIN_SEPARATOR)\n        bytes32 newDomainSeparator = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\"),\n                keccak256(bytes(\"TrailsIntentEntrypoint\")),\n                keccak256(bytes(\"1\")),\n                block.chainid, // NEW chainId = 10001\n                address(entrypoint)\n            )\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"User's DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (with new chainId):\", vm.toString(newDomainSeparator));\n        console.log(\"Contract's DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (immutable, old chainId):\", vm.toString(entrypoint.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR()));\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"MISMATCH\");\n        console.log(\"User signature will be INVALID because:\");\n        console.log(\"- User signs with: DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(chainId=10001)\");\n        console.log(\"- Contract verifies with: DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(chainId=31337) + intentHash(chainId=10001)\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // User signs with NEW chainId (simulating wallet behavior after fork)\n        (uint8 sigV2, bytes32 sigR2, bytes32 sigS2) = \n            _signIntentWithCustomDomainSeparator(\n                newDomainSeparator,\n                user, \n                depositAmount, \n                intentAddress2, \n                deadline, \n                intentNonce2, \n                feeAmount, \n                feeCollector\n            );\n\n        console.log(\"=== ATTEMPTING TRANSACTION ===\");\n        \n        // Try to execute - this will FAIL\n        vm.prank(feeCollector);\n        vm.expectRevert(); // Expect InvalidIntentSignature error\n        entrypoint.depositToIntent(\n            user,\n            address(token),\n            depositAmount,\n            intentAddress2,\n            deadline,\n            intentNonce2,\n            feeAmount,\n            feeCollector,\n            sigV2,\n            sigR2,\n            sigS2\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"Transaction REVERTED\");\n        console.log(\"Error: InvalidIntentSignature\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n    }\n\n    function _signIntent2(\n        address usr,\n        uint256 amt,\n        address intent,\n        uint256 dl,\n        uint256 nonce,\n        uint256 fee,\n        address collector\n    ) internal view returns (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) {\n        bytes32 hash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                entrypoint.TRAILS_INTENT_TYPEHASH(),\n                usr,\n                address(token),\n                amt,\n                intent,\n                dl,\n                block.chainid,\n                nonce,\n                fee,\n                collector\n            )\n        );\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", entrypoint.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), hash));\n        return vm.sign(userPrivateKey, digest);\n    }\n\n    function _signIntentWithCustomDomainSeparator(\n        bytes32 customDomainSeparator,\n        address usr,\n        uint256 amt,\n        address intent,\n        uint256 dl,\n        uint256 nonce,\n        uint256 fee,\n        address collector\n    ) internal view returns (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) {\n        bytes32 hash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                entrypoint.TRAILS_INTENT_TYPEHASH(),\n                usr,\n                address(token),\n                amt,\n                intent,\n                dl,\n                block.chainid, // Uses CURRENT chainId (after fork)\n                nonce,\n                fee,\n                collector\n            )\n        );\n        // Use CUSTOM domain separator (with new chainId) - simulating user wallet behavior\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", customDomainSeparator, hash));\n        return vm.sign(userPrivateKey, digest);\n    }\n\n    function _signPermit(address owner, uint256 permitAmount, uint256 deadline)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s)\n    {\n        bytes32 hash = keccak256(\n            abi.encodePacked(\n                \"\\x19\\x01\",\n                token.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(),\n                keccak256(\n                    abi.encode(\n                        keccak256(\"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"),\n                        owner,\n                        address(entrypoint),\n                        permitAmount,\n                        token.nonces(owner),\n                        deadline\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n        return vm.sign(userPrivateKey, hash);\n    }\n}\n```\nResult:\n```\n> forge test --match-contract TrailsIntentEntrypointTest -vvvv\n[⠊] Compiling...\n[⠒] Compiling 1 files with Solc 0.8.30\n[⠑] Solc 0.8.30 finished in 3.48s\nCompiler run successful!\n\nRan 1 test for test/TrailsIntentEntrypoint.t.sol:TrailsIntentEntrypointTest\n[PASS] test_ChainForkCausesPermanentDoSDueToImmutableDomainSeparator() (gas: 196798)\nLogs:\n  === PHASE 1: BEFORE HARD FORK ===\n  Initial chainId: 31337\n  DOMAIN_SEPARATOR (immutable): 0xf34ed92df5d56